    "title": "Security software discovery",
    "desc": "A process searched the process list or filesystem for security tooling by name - grepping ps output or using pgrep/pidof for EDR, AV, audit and monitoring agents (CrowdStrike/falcond, osquery, Wazuh, SentinelOne, Sysmon, auditbeat/filebeat, ClamAV ...). Enumerating which defender is watching is a standard pre-attack step (MITRE T1518.001): the attacker learns what to evade or disable before acting. Grepping for these specific product names is not something routine automation does, so it is a clean signal.",
